---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/global/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/global/Footer.astro';
import Container from '../../components/global/Container.astro';
import Section from '../../components/global/Section.astro';
import TechnicalLabel from '../../components/global/TechnicalLabel.astro';
import Button from '../../components/global/Button.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Silicon X × AionSi | FPGA Engineering Capacity" description="AionSi engineering alignment for Silicon X across RTL, Design Verification, FPGA validation, Physical Design, DFT and engineering automation, structured around defined work packages and milestones.">
  <Header />
  <main>
    <Section class="bg-[var(--aionsi-surface-alt)] py-14 md:py-20 lg:py-24">
      <Container>
        <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1.08fr_.72fr] lg:items-center">
          <div>
            <TechnicalLabel>SILICON X × AIONSI · ENGINEERING CAPACITY ALIGNMENT</TechnicalLabel>
            <h1 class="mt-4 max-w-5xl text-5xl font-semibold leading-[1.02] tracking-tight text-[var(--aionsi-navy)] md:text-7xl">Extend Silicon X's FPGA engineering capacity.</h1>
            <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-slate-600 md:text-2xl">AionSi supports defined RTL, Design Verification, FPGA validation, Physical Design and DFT work packages with milestone-based engineering ownership.</p>
            <div class="mt-9 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
              <Button href="/contact">Discuss an Engineering Requirement</Button>
              <a href="/capabilities" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center border border-slate-300 px-6 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--aionsi-navy)] transition hover:border-[var(--aionsi-blue)]">Explore Capabilities</a>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-5 text-sm text-slate-500">AionSi management team in Malaysia · 20 September–5 October 2026</p>
          </div>
          <div class="border border-slate-200 bg-white p-7 shadow-sm">
            <TechnicalLabel>PARTNERSHIP MODEL</TechnicalLabel>
            <h2 class="mt-4 text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--aionsi-navy)]">Add execution capacity while Silicon X retains product ownership.</h2>
            <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-slate-600">Start with a defined engineering requirement, prove delivery on a focused work package and scale only when the working model is proven.</p>
            <div class="mt-7 grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--aionsi-navy)]">
              <div class="border border-slate-200 p-4">Defined scope</div>
              <div class="border border-slate-200 p-4">Technical ownership</div>
              <div class="border border-slate-200 p-4">Milestone driven</div>
              <div class="border border-slate-200 p-4">Scalable capacity</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </Container>
    </Section>

    <Section class="py-12 md:py-18">
      <Container>
        <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[.78fr_1.22fr] lg:items-start">
          <div>
            <TechnicalLabel>ENGINEERING CAPACITY</TechnicalLabel>
            <h2 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--aionsi-navy)] md:text-5xl">Additional execution bandwidth across the FPGA product lifecycle.</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-5 text-base leading-8 text-slate-600">
            <p>Silicon X is developing proprietary FPGA products focused on low-latency, low-power and cost-effective programmable logic. Public information indicates that its FPGA has powered on and the company has been progressing through testing and commercialization.</p>
            <p>AionSi can complement that product journey with focused engineering capacity across RTL, Design Verification, FPGA validation, Physical Design, DFT and engineering automation.</p>
            <p class="font-semibold text-[var(--aionsi-navy)]">The objective is not to replace the core Silicon X organization. It is to create an additional execution lane around a specific engineering milestone or work package.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </Container>
    </Section>

    <Section class="bg-white py-12 md:py-18">
      <Container>
        <TechnicalLabel>FPGA ENGINEERING WORKSTREAMS</TechnicalLabel>
        <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-base leading-7 text-slate-600">Engineering coverage aligned to the product path from RTL and verification through implementation and validation.</p>
        <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
          <div class="border border-slate-200 p-7"><div class="text-xs tracking-[.18em] text-[var(--aionsi-orange)]">01 · FRONT END</div><h3 class="mt-4 text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--aionsi-navy)]">RTL & FPGA Design</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">RTL development, IP integration and subsystem execution for defined FPGA product requirements and interfaces.</p></div>
          <div class="border border-slate-200 p-7"><div class="text-xs tracking-[.18em] text-[var(--aionsi-orange)]">02 · VERIFICATION</div><h3 class="mt-4 text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--aionsi-navy)]">Design Verification</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">SystemVerilog/UVM verification, regressions, debug, coverage closure and reusable verification infrastructure.</p></div>
          <div class="border border-slate-200 p-7"><div class="text-xs tracking-[.18em] text-[var(--aionsi-orange)]">03 · VALIDATION</div><h3 class="mt-4 text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--aionsi-navy)]">FPGA Validation & Prototyping</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Prototype bring-up, emulation, firmware interfaces, debug and system-level validation for faster engineering feedback.</p></div>
          <div class="border border-slate-200 p-7"><div class="text-xs tracking-[.18em] text-[var(--aionsi-orange)]">04 · IMPLEMENTATION</div><h3 class="mt-4 text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--aionsi-navy)]">Physical Design</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Synthesis, implementation, timing analysis, closure and signoff-oriented execution for defined blocks or milestones.</p></div>
          <div class="border border-slate-200 p-7"><div class="text-xs tracking-[.18em] text-[var(--aionsi-orange)]">05 · TEST</div><h3 class="mt-4 text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--aionsi-navy)]">DFT</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">DFT implementation and verification support, with scope defined around the product architecture and test requirements.</p></div>
          <div class="border border-slate-200 p-7"><div class="text-xs tracking-[.18em] text-[var(--aionsi-orange)]">06 · PRODUCTIVITY</div><h3 class="mt-4 text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--aionsi-navy)]">Engineering Automation</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Regression, flow automation and AI-assisted engineering productivity aligned with existing development methodology.</p></div>
        </div>
      </Container>
    </Section>

    <Section class="bg-[var(--aionsi-surface-alt)] py-12 md:py-18">
      <Container>
        <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[.7fr_1.3fr] lg:items-start">
          <div><TechnicalLabel>EXAMPLE WORK PACKAGES</TechnicalLabel><h2 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--aionsi-navy)] md:text-5xl">Assign a concrete engineering unit of work.</h2><p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-slate-600">AionSi teams can be structured around an agreed scope, interface, milestone and acceptance criteria.</p></div>
          <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
            <div class="border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--aionsi-navy)]">FPGA Verification</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">UVM environment, testbench development, regressions, coverage and debug.</p></div>
            <div class="border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--aionsi-navy)]">RTL / IP Integration</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">RTL development, IP integration and subsystem implementation around defined interfaces.</p></div>
            <div class="border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--aionsi-navy)]">Implementation Closure</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Synthesis, P&R, STA, timing closure and ECO support for agreed blocks or milestones.</p></div>
            <div class="border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--aionsi-navy)]">DFT Engineering</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">DFT implementation and verification activities defined around product test requirements.</p></div>
            <div class="border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--aionsi-navy)]">FPGA Validation</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Prototype bring-up, debug, firmware interfaces and system-level validation.</p></div>
            <div class="border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--aionsi-navy)]">Verification Automation</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Regression infrastructure, scripting and engineering productivity improvements.</p></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </Container>
    </Section>

    <Section class="py-12 md:py-18">
      <Container>
        <TechnicalLabel>RELEVANT AIONSI ENGINEERING EVIDENCE</TechnicalLabel>
        <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-base leading-7 text-slate-600">Selected engineering areas available for technical review during an initial discussion.</p>
        <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
          <div class="border border-slate-200 p-7"><div class="text-xs tracking-[.18em] text-[var(--aionsi-orange)]">01 · INTERFACES</div><h3 class="mt-4 text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--aionsi-navy)]">High-Speed Interface Verification</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Reusable UVM architecture and protocol-focused verification approaches for high-speed interfaces, including PCIe-oriented work.</p></div>
          <div class="border border-slate-200 p-7"><div class="text-xs tracking-[.18em] text-[var(--aionsi-orange)]">02 · MEMORY</div><h3 class="mt-4 text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--aionsi-navy)]">Advanced Memory Verification</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Verification approaches for advanced memory subsystems, including HBM-focused interface and subsystem verification considerations.</p></div>
          <div class="border border-slate-200 p-7"><div class="text-xs tracking-[.18em] text-[var(--aionsi-orange)]">03 · SOC</div><h3 class="mt-4 text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--aionsi-navy)]">Multi-Subsystem SoC Verification</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">End-to-end verification approaches across subsystem integration, regressions, debug, planning and closure.</p></div>
          <div class="border border-slate-200 p-7"><div class="text-xs tracking-[.18em] text-[var(--aionsi-orange)]">04 · FORMAL</div><h3 class="mt-4 text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--aionsi-navy)]">Formal Verification</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Property-based verification and formal-analysis workflows using tools such as Cadence JasperGold for targeted closure tasks.</p></div>
        </div>
      </Container>
    </Section>

    <Section class="py-12 md:py-18">
      <Container>
        <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[.75fr_1.25fr]">
          <div><TechnicalLabel>DELIVERY MODEL</TechnicalLabel><h2 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--aionsi-navy)] md:text-5xl">From engineering requirement to delivered work package.</h2></div>
          <div class="grid gap-3">
            <div class="border-b border-slate-200 py-5"><div class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--aionsi-orange)]">01 · UNDERSTAND</div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Clarify product stage, architecture, block or subsystem, tools, interfaces and milestone.</p></div>
            <div class="border-b border-slate-200 py-5"><div class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--aionsi-orange)]">02 · DEFINE</div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Agree scope, skills, tools, deliverables, ownership boundaries and acceptance criteria.</p></div>
            <div class="border-b border-slate-200 py-5"><div class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--aionsi-orange)]">03 · BUILD</div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Assign engineers with the required semiconductor, verification and implementation experience.</p></div>
            <div class="border-b border-slate-200 py-5"><div class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--aionsi-orange)]">04 · EXECUTE</div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Deliver against agreed technical milestones, quality gates and engineering KPIs, with regular technical reviews.</p></div>
            <div class="py-5"><div class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--aionsi-orange)]">05 · VALIDATE & HANDOFF</div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Review outputs, close open items and complete documentation and knowledge transfer.</p></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </Container>
    </Section>

    <Section class="bg-[var(--aionsi-surface-alt)] py-12 md:py-18">
      <Container>
        <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[.7fr_1.3fr] lg:items-start">
          <div><TechnicalLabel>ENGAGEMENT PATH</TechnicalLabel><h2 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--aionsi-navy)] md:text-5xl">Start with one work package. Scale after proven delivery.</h2></div>
          <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
            <div class="border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--aionsi-navy)]">Parallel execution</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Create an additional engineering lane without changing core product ownership.</p></div>
            <div class="border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--aionsi-navy)]">Specialist capacity</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Add focused semiconductor expertise around a specific technical bottleneck or milestone.</p></div>
            <div class="border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--aionsi-navy)]">Milestone support</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Structure delivery around verification closure, implementation targets, validation or product milestones.</p></div>
            <div class="border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--aionsi-navy)]">Scale after validation</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Expand from a focused team to dedicated engineering capacity when collaboration and delivery are proven.</p></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-10 grid items-center gap-4 border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 md:grid-cols-7">
          <div><div class="text-xs tracking-[.18em] text-[var(--aionsi-orange)]">01</div><div class="mt-2 font-semibold text-[var(--aionsi-navy)]">Work Package</div></div>
          <div class="hidden text-center text-slate-300 md:block">→</div>
          <div><div class="text-xs tracking-[.18em] text-[var(--aionsi-orange)]">02</div><div class="mt-2 font-semibold text-[var(--aionsi-navy)]">Focused Team</div></div>
          <div class="hidden text-center text-slate-300 md:block">→</div>
          <div><div class="text-xs tracking-[.18em] text-[var(--aionsi-orange)]">03</div><div class="mt-2 font-semibold text-[var(--aionsi-navy)]">Milestone Delivery</div></div>
          <div class="hidden text-center text-slate-300 md:block">→</div>
          <div><div class="text-xs tracking-[.18em] text-[var(--aionsi-orange)]">04</div><div class="mt-2 font-semibold text-[var(--aionsi-navy)]">Scale</div></div>
        </div>
      </Container>
    </Section>

    <Section class="bg-[var(--aionsi-navy)] py-14 md:py-20">
      <Container>
        <div class="max-w-4xl">
          <TechnicalLabel>FOR SILICON X ENGINEERING LEADERS</TechnicalLabel>
          <h2 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white md:text-6xl">Let's identify one engineering work package to evaluate together.</h2>
          <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-slate-300">Share the engineering requirement, current milestone and expected deliverable. AionSi can map the required skills, team structure and delivery model around it.</p>
          <div class="mt-8"><Button href="/contact">Discuss the Work Package</Button></div>
        </div>
      </Container>
    </Section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
